    "lawCode": "Amd §44, add §224-b, Pub Serv L; add §399-zz, Gen Bus L",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4192B\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the public service law and the general business law,\nin relation to requiring utility corporations, energy service\ncompanies, municipalities, telephone corporations and cable television\ncompanies to provide large-print versions of billing statements upon\nrequest by the consumer\n\n PURPOSE :\nTo require that telephone, cable, utility, and municipal bills be\noffered in a larger font size, in electronic and paper format, to\naccommodate visually impaired and elderly customers.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nThis legislation amends section 44 of the public service law by adding\nsubdivision 5, adds section 399-zz to the general business law, and\nadds section 224-b to the public service law.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nBills for services provided are often written in small print,\nespecially added fees and charges, making understanding the charges\ncomplicated and difficult. Some of my constituents have expressed a\ndesire to receive bills highlighting the charges in a larger font size\nso they are able to fully understand their bills. This legislation\ndoes not mandate that companies immediately change their billing\nsystems.  Instead, it requires that these companies make this new\nservice available to customers who send a written request for larger\nfont bills.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nThis is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect April 1 ,2010; provided however, that this\nact shall not apply to any utility corporation, energy services\ncompany, municipality, telephone corporation, or cable television\ncompany that services less than 50,000 customers in the state until\nNovember 1, 2010; provided, however that effective immediately, the\naddition, amendment and/or repeal of any rule or regulation necessary\nfor the implementation of this act on its effective date are\nauthorized and directed to be made and completed on or before such\neffective date.\n",
